Give OHOS its own system permission PlatformHandle.

Turning on os_level_geolocation_permission_supported for OHOS left the port on
system_permission_settings_default.cc, whose handle answers every question
wrong in a way that is worse than it looks:

  bool IsAllowed(ContentSettingsType) override { return true; }
  void OpenSystemSettings(...) override { NOTREACHED(); }
  void Request(...) override { NOTREACHED(); }
  std::unique_ptr<ScopedObservation> Observe(...) override { return nullptr; }

The two NOTREACHED()s are traps in this build. Request() is reachable from the
<permission> element with no platform gating in front of it, so a page can take
the browser down. OpenSystemSettings() backs the content-settings bubble's
primary button.

The ordering matters and is not obvious. IsAllowed() returning true
unconditionally is what currently keeps the bubble from ever being built --
InitializeSystemGeolocationPermissionBubble() runs only when IsAllowed() is
false -- so it is the door in front of that trap. Making IsAllowed() tell the
truth on its own would promote a quiet wrong answer into a reliable crash.
Both change here, together.

The OHOS handle answers from the state the shell reports, and only for the
permissions the shell actually manages: for anything else it defers to the
default's answers, because claiming a capability is blocked when nothing has
established that would suppress prompts the user should still see.
OpenSystemSettings and Request go back to the shell through closures the
runtime bridge installs, since PlatformHandle is built below
//chrome/browser:core and cannot call up into it. Observe returns the
GeolocationObservation that the buildflag already brings into this target.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51.

Apply with:
  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-system-permission-handle.patch

diff --git a/chrome/browser/permissions/system/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/permissions/system/BUILD.gn
--- a/chrome/browser/permissions/system/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/permissions/system/BUILD.gn
@@ -71,6 +71,12 @@
       "system_permission_settings_win.cc",
     ]
     deps += [ "//chrome/browser:browser_public_dependencies" ]
+  } else if (is_ohos) {
+    sources += [
+      "system_permission_settings_ohos.cc",
+      "system_permission_settings_ohos.h",
+    ]
+    deps += [ "//chrome/browser:browser_public_dependencies" ]
   } else {
     sources += [ "system_permission_settings_default.cc" ]
   }
